  "summary": "Russia's oldest lacquer miniatures: oil painting in transparent glazes on black boxes near Moscow.",
  "description": "Founded in 1795 around Korobov's visor factory, Fedoskino perfected miniature oil painting in layered transparent glazes over mother-of-pearl or gold-foil inlays — portraits, landscapes and scenes of peasant and town life glowing with a shell undertone, on snuffboxes, cigarette cases and trinket boxes of pressed papier-mâché lacquered to mirror depth. Realism is the school's signature: tinted shadows, luminous skies, theatrical lamplight. Fedoskino's academy still trains Russia's lacquer painters beside the Palekh and Mstyora schools it inspired.",
